            <ArticleTitle>Rectus sheath haematoma: an anticoagulation dilemma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>94-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Rectus sheath haematoma (RSH) is an uncommon condition with a propensity for difficult and mistaken diagnosis. We describe a case where management was complicated by the patient's requirement for anticoagulation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
